# Line-ending policy for Balance Manager (Windows host, Git autocrlf=true).
#
# Without this file, Git had to guess: it checked files out with CRLF, but a
# tool could rewrite one with LF and `git status` would then flag it forever
# even though no text changed (this bit .gitignore / gradlew.bat / e2e scripts
# in Oct 2026). These rules make the endings explicit so the guesswork
# -- and the phantom "modified" state -- cannot come back.

# Normalize all text files to LF inside the repository; convert on checkout.
* text=auto

# Windows scripts and command tools must keep CRLF even when a checkout or
# tool rewrites them.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touch these formats' endings at all.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.apk binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
